 the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 97 at 14 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled  Skin  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm longitudinal portion of skin excised to a depth of 0 3cm  No discrete lesions are noted on the surface  The specimen is trisected and submitted entirely in cassette A  Labeled  Breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm white stellate nodule  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1 and resubmitted in cassette K  The remainder of the nodule is submitted in cassttes B   F  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes H   J  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Yes.
