Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 42 CLINICAL DATA  1 4cm invasive ductal carcinoma  excised elsewhere and reviewed here                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MULTIPLE FOCI IN THE REGION OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The largest focus of residual invasive carcinoma spans 0 5cm and is 0 2cm from the resection margin  No definite lymphatic invasion is seen  BREAST  LEFT  NEW DEEP MARGIN    BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  PRESENT IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  NOTE  Tumor is confined to the lymph node  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in three parts are the following   1   left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x d1 0cm lymph node  sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm well circumscribed tan white fleshy nodule within the parenchyma  The specimen is trisected and submitted entirely in A and B  Labeled  left breast   is a 5  x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x0 6cm overlying skin ellipse and a 2 9cm well healed linear scar  The specimen is oriented with a long suture indicating the lateral margin and a short suture indicating the superior margin  The specimen is sectioned medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm healing biopsy cavity with surrounding fibrosis and fat necrosis which extends 0 3cm from the deep resection margin  0 6cm from the medial resection margin  2 5cm from the lateral resection margin  0 4cm from the superior resection margin  and 0 3cm from the inferior resection margin  The biopsy cavity is present 0 8cm beneath the skin surface  No other lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  C  biopsy cavity and deep margin D  biopsy cavity and superior margin E  biopsy cavity and inferior margin F  biopsy cavity and overlying skin G  representative section of biopsy cavity Labeled  left breast  new deep margin  stitch marks deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch orienting one surface  The