ormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 97 at 08 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number in two parts  Labeled  right breast and axillary contents  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  which is covered by REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm ellipse of unremarkable skin with unremarkable nipple with no apparent scars  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 3 7cm lobulated white tan  focally necrotic tumor 2 0cm from the posterior margin  A section of tumor with the closest margin is submitted in A  Additional samples of tumor are submitted in B D  Samples of unremarkable parenchyma are submitted in E F  A sample of unremarkable skeletal muscle measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm is submitted in G  Lymph nodes are submitted in H P  Labeled  highest axillary node  is a piece of fatty tissue with a lymph node measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  submitted entirely in Q  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  HIGHEST RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISION   report_end  , Yes.
